## Section C: The Shadbala System (Vedic Parallel)

### Overview

**Shadbala** ("sixfold strength") is the Vedic equivalent to Western strength calculation, evaluating planets through six dimensions rather than a simple point total.

### Six Components of Shadbala

| Component | What It Measures |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Sthana Bala** | Positional strength (sign placement: exaltation, own sign, friendly, enemy, debilitated) |
| **Dig Bala** | Directional strength (Sun & Mars strong in 10th; Moon & Venus in 4th; Mercury & Jupiter in 1st; Saturn in 7th) |
| **Kala Bala** | Temporal strength (day/night, lunar phase, planetary hour, age considerations) |
| **Cheshta Bala** | Motional strength (speed, retrograde vs. direct) |
| **Naisargika Bala** | Natural/inherent strength (Sun, Moon, Jupiter inherently strong; Mars, Saturn inherently weaker) |
| **Drik Bala** | Aspectual strength (benefic vs. malefic aspects; conjunction with nodes) |

**Strength Ranges:** 
- High Shadbala (6+ Rupas): Planet expresses positively
- Moderate (4-6 Rupas): Mixed effects
- Low (<4 Rupas): Weak expression, may require remedial work

